'''argufy''' (är′gū-fī), ''v.''; pret. and pp. ''argufied'', ppr. ''argufying''. [Improp. < ''argue'' + ''-fy''.] '''I.''' ''intrans.'' '''1.''' To argue, commonly in a pertinacious manner, or for the sake of controversy; wrangle.
