'''argulid''' (är′gū-lid), ''n.'' A fish-louse of the family ''Argulidæ''.

'''Argulidæ''' (är-gū′li-dē), ''n. pl.'' [NL., < ''Argulus'' + ''-idæ''.] A family of siphonostomous entomostracan crustaceans, typified by the genus ''Argulus''. {{smaller|These fish-lice have a flat shield-like body, the cephalothorax coalesced with the abdomen, and the postabdomen rudimentary and bearing two tail-fins. They are parasitic on various fishes, especially fresh-water species, and sometimes attack young fishes in such numbers as to cause their death. The family with some authors constitutes a suborder ''Branchiura''.}}

